/-!
# Final local calculations for MS93 (4.4)

Both local calculations of (4.4.5) are proved on the actual extended path,
including the radius-image boundary at b=8. Quotient-action recognition gives
the full natural section and the genuine moving-span containment. The selected
product at the predecessor edge then supplies local centrality, b=8 and both
edge indices, without the incompatible legacy successor-edge certificate.

`SourceIntegration` assembles every final (4.4) clause from CommonFacts, b>4,
the earlier local control and critical-prefix exclusion, prescribed replacement,
and an actual extended path. It derives b>6 from a regular window, transports
the moving span to any M-vertex, proves |H|<=4, and fills CoreFactors.Earlier.
The DistanceEight parent retains construction of the earlier LocalCommutator
and RegularPaths inputs. No unconditional source theorem is asserted here.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed pp.894--895.
-/
